    "title": "41st annual Late Night in the Phog announced by Kansas Athletics - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Keller Welton ,\n53 minutes ago\nLAWRENCE ( KSNT ) – The 41st annual Late Night in the Phog will feature dueling DJs in lieu of a musical artist.\nLate Night is set for Friday, Oct. 17, at 6:30 p.m. inside historic Allen Fieldhouse. The night will begin with women’s basketball team scrimmaging, followed by entertainers including the Rock Chalk spirit squad, the KU basketball band, spirit squad and fan favorite halfcourt shot to win $10,000.\nKansas group preserves and restores historic stonework Then the men’s team will scrimmage, offering fans the first look at the new squad featuring the top-rated recruit in the nation, Darryn Peterson. Peterson is the third No. 1 recruit to play under coach Bill Self, joining Andrew Wiggins and Josh Jackson.\nFollowing the scrimmage will be the very first Late Night After Party, a KU student-only dance party on the Allen Fieldhouse court featuring dueling DJs. The event will continue to be free for fans, however tickets will need to be claimed online in advance and seating outside the student section will be reserved.\nFor more local news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news in northeast Kansas by downloading our mobile app and by signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track Weather app by clicking here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSNT 27 News.",
